  "shortDescription": "Spread the word ACORNS are a SUPERFOOD! Low gluten & high antioxidants. Spearheading green economy.",
  "projectStory": "Project story\nCreator\nMarcie Mayer\nmore infocontact\nCategory\nEnvironment\nTags\nother\nBacking information\nCrowdfunding risks\nlearn more\nMouthwateringly Tantalizing\nAcorn Cookies and other great perks \nfor your contribution!\nA plethora of information at www.iloveacorns.com!\nThe Acorn Center is ready to open if we can get a new roof! The Hamada Acorn Initiative creates sustainable income from an ancient oak forest for farm families in Greece where the economic crisis has hit hardest.\nThe World's 1st Acorn Bakery\nSweet & Savoury, Low and Zero Gluten Treats will show the world just how versatile acorns can be. Acorn tortillas, pan bread, muffins, cookies, pudding, jelly and much more will be served with local organic ingredients.\nQuercus Ithaburensis  (Valonia Oak) have giant acorns up to 40g each! \n\n\n2012 film for even more information about the Acorn Adventure on Kea:\n\n(GREEK version on the Gallery page)\n\n\n \nhttp://www.huffingtonpost.com/marisa-churchill/i-love-acorns_b_4395356.html\n\n\nWe will continue to offer FREE adult and children's seminars as well as our 1/2 day activities for schools from the mainland. Here are the connections we've already made:\n\n\n \nGreek and International Press for the Acorn Initiative:\n\n\n \nThank you for taking a few minutes out of your day to watch Natasha Blatsiou's 4 minute film about the Acorn Initiative on Kea. We hope it made you smile!\n\n\nClick the GALLERY tab at the top for 3 more videos about Oaks and Acorns on Kea.",
